    <h3 class="mgdb-leaf-heading mgdb-spaced" id="gene-xref">Gene model cross-references and pan-genes</h3>
    <p class="gene-leaf-lead">How a gene model in one annotation relates to gene models in the others&#58; the cross-reference files map identifiers between B73 assemblies, and the pan-gene analysis groups models across every annotation by sequence similarity and syntenic position.</p>
    <div class="gene-panel">
      <p>Please note that there is not a 1-to-1 correspondence between all gene models in all annotations. Some gene models are unique to specific genome assemblies, some have been split or merged between annotation or assembly versions, some direct associations may be difficult to calculate, so multiple gene models that are similar in sequence and position may be listed. And some gene models may be similar in sequence but do not appear in the same syntenic locations.</p>
      <details class="gene-details">
        <summary>Click to learn more</summary>
        <p>The rules for associating gene models across assemblies require not only close sequence similarity, but also that they both appear in syntenic positions. Because of this, there are gene models that are not associated with all gene models in the current representative assembly annotation in spite of exact or near exact sequence similarity. This is often due to unplaced scaffolds that contain gene models.</p>
        <p>There are multiple ways to define and generate a pan-genome. Here we use "pan-gene" to mean to an analysis of multiple genome annotations to group gene models by sequence similarity and syntenic position, to identify core gene models \(present in all annotations\) and to identify orphan gene models \(present in only one\).</p>
      </details>
      <ul class="gene-link-list">
        <li><a href="https://download.maizegdb.org/Pan-genes/B73_gene_xref/">Gene model associations across all B73 assemblies</a>.</li>
        <li><a href="https://download.maizegdb.org/Pan-genes/Pan-Zea">Current pan-gene data</a></li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <h3 class="mgdb-leaf-heading mgdb-spaced" id="gene-insertions">Insertion data sets</h3>
    <p class="gene-leaf-lead">Transposon insertion collections mapped onto gene models, for finding a mutant allele of a gene of interest. Each release is given against the assemblies it was mapped to, so pick the one matching the annotation you are working in.</p>
    <div class="mgdb-card-grid gene-download-grid gene-insertion-grid">
      <article class="mgdb-card">
        <h3>UniformMu</h3>
        <p>A public reverse-genetics resource of sequence-indexed <i>Mutator</i> insertions in a uniform W22 background. Insertions are mapped onto gene models, so a gene of interest can be matched to the stocks that carry a likely knockout allele of it and those stocks ordered from the Stock Center.</p>
        <ul class="gene-link-list">
          <li><a href="/uniformmu">About the UniformMu project</a></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mgdb-small"><b>Zm-B73-REFERENCE-NAM-5.0</b></p>
        <ul class="gene-link-list">
          <li><a href="https://download.maizegdb.org/Insertions/UniformMu/UniformMu_Release-9_B73v5_gene_models.xlsx">Release 9 Excel spreadsheet</a></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mgdb-small"><b>Zm-B73-REFERENCE-GRAMENE-4.0</b></p>
        <ul class="gene-link-list">
          <li><a href="https://download.maizegdb.org/Insertions/UniformMu/UniformMu_Release-9_B73v4.xlsx">Release 9 Excel spreadsheet</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://download.maizegdb.org/Insertions/UniformMu/UniformMu_Release-9_B73v4_exons.xlsx">Release 9 Excel spreadsheet</a> with gene structure</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mgdb-small"><b>B73 RefGen_v3</b></p>
        <ul class="gene-link-list">
          <li><a href="https://download.maizegdb.org/Insertions/UniformMu/UniformMu_Release-8_GeneModel_B73_RefGen_v3.xlsx">Release 8 Excel spreadsheet</a> &#8212; Filtered Gene Set, gene models with insertions</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mgdb-small"><b>B73 RefGen_v2</b></p>
        <ul class="gene-link-list">
          <li><a href="https://download.maizegdb.org/Insertions/UniformMu/UniformMu_Release-7_Insertions_in_RefGenv2_FGS.xlsx">Release 7</a> and <a href="https://download.maizegdb.org/Insertions/UniformMu/UniformMu_Release-8_Insertions_in_RefGenv2_FGS.xlsx">Release 8</a> Excel spreadsheets &#8212; Filtered Gene Set, insertions within 100 bp of a gene model</li>
          <li><a href="https://download.maizegdb.org/Insertions/UniformMu/UniformMu_Release-7_Insertions_in_RefGenv2_FGS_exons.xlsx">Release 7</a> and <a href="https://download.maizegdb.org/Insertions/UniformMu/UniformMu_Release-8_Insertions_in_RefGenv2_FGS_exons.xlsx">Release 8</a> Excel spreadsheets &#8212; Filtered Gene Set, insertions in exons</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mgdb-small"><b>W22 to B73</b></p>
        <ul class="gene-link-list">
          <li><a href="https://download.maizegdb.org/Insertions/UniformMu/UniformMu_W22_V4_lookup.xlsx">Cross-reference Excel spreadsheet</a></li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="mgdb-card">
        <h3>BonnMu</h3>
        <p>A sequence-indexed collection of <i>Mutator</i> transposon insertions from the Crop Functional Genomics group at the University of Bonn, mapped onto B73 gene models so a gene of interest can be matched to the lines carrying an insertion in it. The fifth release was made in February 2024.</p>
        <ul class="gene-link-list">
          <li><a href="https://www.inres.uni-bonn.de/cfg/en/c-f-g/research/bonnmu" target="_blank" rel="noopener">About the BonnMu project</a></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mgdb-small"><b>Releases</b></p>
        <ul class="gene-link-list">
          <li><a href="https://download.maizegdb.org/Insertions/BonnMu/BonnMu_5th_Release_2024-02-29.xlsx">5th release Excel spreadsheet</a> \(February 2024\)</li>
          <li><a href="https://download.maizegdb.org/Insertions/BonnMu/BonnMu_4th_Release_2021-03-18.xlsx">4th release Excel spreadsheet</a> \(March 2021\)</li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="mgdb-card">
        <h3>Ac/Ds-GFP</h3>
        <p>A genome-wide collection of <i>Ac/Ds</i> transposon launch platforms, each carrying a GFP marker that makes its transposition visible in the kernel. Because a <i>Ds</i> element moves preferentially to sites near where it started, a platform close to a gene of interest can be used to raise a local series of insertions in it.</p>
        <ul class="gene-link-list">
          <li><a href="/projects/dooner_du_acds">About the Dooner &amp; Du Ac/Ds-GFP project</a></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mgdb-small"><b>Validated insertions</b> &mdash; <a href="/data_center/reference/9043193">Warman et al., 2020</a></p>
        <ul class="gene-link-list">
          <li><a href="https://download.maizegdb.org/Insertions/AcDs_Dooner/">Validation table with B73 v3 and v4 gene model assignments</a></li>
        </ul>
      </article>

      <article class="mgdb-card">
        <h3>Ac/Ds \(Vollbrecht\)</h3>
        <p>A collection of sequenced <i>Ds</i> insertion sites generated from <i>Ac</i>-mobilised <i>Ds</i> elements, reported with their flanking sequence so an insertion can be placed against a gene model.</p>
        <ul class="gene-link-list">
          <li><a href="https://doi.org/10.1105/tpc.109.073452" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Vollbrecht et al., 2010, <i>The Plant Cell</i></a></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mgdb-small"><b>Zm-B73-REFERENCE-NAM-5.0</b></p>
        <ul class="gene-link-list">
          <li><a href="https://download.maizegdb.org/Insertions/AcDs_Vollbrecht/AcDs_B73_v5_gene_models.xlsx">Insertions with gene model assignments, Excel spreadsheet</a></li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mgdb-small"><b>B73 RefGen_v3</b></p>
        <ul class="gene-link-list">
          <li><a href="https://download.maizegdb.org/Insertions/AcDs_Vollbrecht/AcDs_B73v3.gff3">Insertion positions, GFF3</a></li>
        </ul>
      </article>
    </div>

    <h3 class="mgdb-leaf-heading mgdb-spaced" id="gene-older">Older gene model downloads</h3>
    <p class="gene-leaf-lead">Gene model files for superseded B73 annotations, kept so a published analysis can be reproduced against the set it was built on.</p>
    <div class="mgdb-card-grid gene-download-grid gene-older-grid">
      <article class="mgdb-card">
        <h3>Zm00001d.2 &#8211; Zm-B73-REFERENCE-GRAMENE-4.0</h3>
        <p class="mgdb-small">Gene model set <b>Zm00001d.2</b> corresponds to Gramene release 36.</p>
        <ul class="gene-link-list">
          <li><a href="https://download.maizegdb.org/Zm-B73-REFERENCE-GRAMENE-4.0/Zm-B73-REFERENCE-GRAMENE-4.0_Zm00001d.2.cDNA.fa.gz">Zm00001d.2 gene model cDNA fasta</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://download.maizegdb.org/Zm-B73-REFERENCE-GRAMENE-4.0/Zm-B73-REFERENCE-GRAMENE-4.0_Zm00001d.2.ncrna.fa.gz">Zm00001d.2 gene model ncRNA fasta</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://download.maizegdb.org/Zm-B73-REFERENCE-GRAMENE-4.0/Zm-B73-REFERENCE-GRAMENE-4.0_Zm00001d.2.protein.fa.gz">Zm00001d.2 gene model translations fasta</a></li>
          <li><a href="https://download.maizegdb.org/Zm-B73-REFERENCE-GRAMENE-4.0/Zm-B73-REFERENCE-GRAMENE-4.0_Zm00001d.2.gff3.gz">Zm00001d.2 gene model GFF3</a></li>
